    "title": "UConn vs. Illinois box score: Full stats from 2026 Final Four basketball game",
    "text": "UConn vs. Illinois box score: Full stats from 2026 Final Four basketball game originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.After 40 minutes, the No. 2 UConn Huskies are heading back to their third title game in four seasons.AdvertisementThe Huskies took care of the No. 3 Fighting Illini 71-62 in a game that showed shooting troubles for both teams. The Huskies shot only 35% from the field and 36% from beyond the arc. Illinois couldn't meet either of these marks, shooting 34% from the field along with a 23% mark from three.Fighting Illini star freshman Keaton Wagler led all scorers with 20 points (7/16 FG, 2/10 3P), along with pitching in eight rebounds and two assists. Despite not scoring much in the second half, Tarris Reed Jr. and Braylon Mullins led the scoring for the Huskies. Reed earned his third double-double of this year's tournament with 17 points (6/12 FG) and 11 boards, while Mullins shot 5/14 (4/7 3P) for 15 points, along with three assists and two steals. Despite scoring in single digits, junior guard Silas Demary Jr. filled the score sheet. He finished with seven points (2/8 FG, 1/6 3P), nine rebounds, seven assists, and two steals en route to victory.UConn will take on the victor of No. 1 Arizona and No. 1 Michigan on Monday at the home field of the Indianapolis Colts.AdvertisementUConn statsStarterMINPTSREBASTSTLBLKFGM-FGA3PM-3PAFTM-FTAPFAlex Karaban35944111-81-76-61Tarris Reed Jr.3517110006-120-05-53Braylon Mullins301530205-144-71-13Silas Demary Jr.31797202-81-62-34Solo Ball281302005-113-70-01BenchMINPTSREBASTSTLBLKFGM-FGA3PM-3PAFTM-FTAPFJayden Ross20710102-42-21-21Eric Reibe5010000-10-00-03Malachi Smith9011000-00-00-04Jaylin Stewart7310001-41-40-01Illinois statsStarterMINPTSREBASTSTLBLKFGM-FGA3PM-3PAFTM-FTAPFDavid Mirkovic28650032-71-31-23Jake Davis17220100-10-12-21Tomislav Ivisic331670114-112-76-64Keaton Wagler372082007-162-104-53Kylan Boswell24660001-60-14-42BenchMINPTSREBASTST